# PneumoScan Frontend — Cursor Rules

Source of truth: `docs/pneumonia-detection-app-design.md`. When in doubt, read that file before changing UI, flows, or tokens.

## Stack

- Next.js App Router (`app/`), React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
- Fonts: Inter (UI), IBM Plex Serif (report/display titles), JetBrains Mono (MRNs, timestamps)
- Icons: `material-icons-round` only (never `material-icons`)
- Route transitions: wrap page content in `<ViewTransition>` from `react`
- Package manager: pnpm

## Design principles

- Premium clarity: calm, spacious, human — white surfaces on a mist canvas, soft depth, smooth motion
- Trust signals: signatures, credentials, timestamps, and certification are first-class UI
- Progressive disclosure: summary first, detail on demand
- Zero-ambiguity CTAs: verb phrases like "Sign Report", "Upload & Run AI Analysis" — never bare "Submit" or "OK"
- Clinical error states: say what failed and what to do next

## Color palette — Clear Blue & White

Use Tailwind tokens (`pneumo-*`, `clinical-*`) or shared CSS utilities — avoid one-off purple/dark hex values.

| Token | Hex | Use |
|---|---|---|
| Canvas White | `#FFFFFF` | Cards, sidebar, panels (`pneumo-surface`) |
| Mist | `#F8FAFC` | Page background (`pneumo-bg-light`) |
| Cloud Border | `#E2E8F0` | Borders, dividers (`pneumo-border`) |
| Primary Blue | `#2563EB` | Buttons, links, active nav (`pneumo-primary`) |
| Blue Hover | `#1D4ED8` | Primary hover (`pneumo-primary-hover`) |
| Sky Tint | `#EFF6FF` | Active/selected fills (`pneumo-sky`) |
| Ink | `#0F172A` | Primary text (`pneumo-ink`, `pneumo-ghost`) |
| Slate Muted | `#64748B` | Secondary text (`pneumo-muted`, `clinical-muted`) |
| Emerald | `#10B981` | Clear / approved (`clinical-mint`) |
| Amber | `#F59E0B` | Suspected / pending (`clinical-amber`) |
| Red | `#EF4444` | Pneumonia detected / urgent only (`clinical-red`) |

- Red is only for positive pneumonia findings and urgent flags — not generic validation errors
- Auth hero panels and premium CTAs may use gradient `from-[#2563EB] to-[#1D4ED8]`
- App theme is light; do not reintroduce the old dark purple palette

## Typography

- Page titles: 24px semibold Ink
- Card headers: 18px semibold Ink
- Body: 14px regular, line-height 1.6
- Labels: `.label-clinical` — 11px uppercase, tracking 0.05em, Slate Muted
- IDs / timestamps: `.mono-data` — JetBrains Mono 13px

## Spacing, layout, elevation

- Base unit: 4px; dashboard max-width 1280px; sidebar 240px fixed
- Cards: `.card-panel` or `.premium-card` (Level 1 soft shadow)
- Shadows: `shadow-soft-1`, `shadow-soft-2`, `shadow-blue-glow` from Tailwind config
- Border radius: inputs 8px (`rounded-sm`), buttons/cards 12–16px (`rounded-md` / `rounded-lg`), pills `rounded-full`

## Reuse these CSS utilities (globals.css)

- Surfaces: `.card-panel`, `.premium-card`, `.glass-panel`
- Forms: `.field-label`, `.input-field`
- Buttons: `.btn-primary`, `.btn-secondary`, `.btn-danger`, `.btn-ghost`
- Badges: `.badge-status` + `.badge-ai-ready | .badge-in-review | .badge-signed | .badge-certified | .badge-flagged`
- AI chips: `.ai-result` + `.ai-detected | .ai-suspected | .ai-clear`
- Prefer components `StatusBadge` and `AiResultBadge` from `components/dashboard/badges.tsx`

Status badges and AI indicators must pair color with an icon — never color-only signalling.

## Project structure

```
app/
  page.tsx                    Landing
  login/, signup/, register-hospital/
  dashboard/                  Doctor shell
    page.tsx                  Overview
    patients/, create/, upload/, analysis/, report/, records/, settings/
  dashboard/admin/            Hospital admin shell (Sidebar variant="admin")
    page.tsx, cosign/, doctors/, audit/

components/
  navigation.tsx              Landing navbar (hidden on /dashboard, /login, /signup, /register-hospital via NavigationGuard)
  auth/                       Login, signup, register-hospital, AuthAside
  dashboard/
    shell.tsx                 DashboardShell — use for all dashboard pages
    sidebar.tsx               variant: "doctor" | "admin"
    page-header.tsx           Eyebrow, title, back link, actions
    badges.tsx                StatusBadge, AiResultBadge
```

## Implementation rules

- New dashboard pages: wrap in `<ViewTransition>`, use `<DashboardShell>`, use `<PageHeader>`, prefer `.card-panel` sections
- Do not show the landing `<Navigation />` on dashboard or auth routes — `NavigationGuard` handles this
- Link CTAs to real routes (`/login`, `/register-hospital`, `/dashboard/upload`, etc.)
- Forms: always `htmlFor`/`id`, meaningful `aria-*` on toggles and icon-only buttons
- Focus: blue ring `#2563EB` / 4px glow on focus-visible (already in globals)
- Keep diffs minimal; match existing naming, imports (`@/components/...`), and file patterns
- Do not add dependencies or refactor unrelated code unless asked
- Do not create git commits unless the user explicitly requests them

## Screen reference (design doc §6)

| Screen | Route |
|---|---|
| Login | `/login` |
| Doctor register | `/signup` |
| Register hospital | `/register-hospital` |
| Doctor dashboard | `/dashboard` |
| Patient list | `/dashboard/patients` |
| Patient registration | `/dashboard/create` |
| X-ray upload + processing | `/dashboard/upload` |
| AI analysis results | `/dashboard/analysis` |
| Report composition / sign-off | `/dashboard/report` |
| Scan records | `/dashboard/records` |
| Settings | `/dashboard/settings` |
| Hospital admin overview | `/dashboard/admin` |
| Co-sign | `/dashboard/admin/cosign` |
| Doctor management | `/dashboard/admin/doctors` |
| Audit log | `/dashboard/admin/audit` |
